ies face symmetric situation, subjunctive dependence — policy to defect gives 4, cooperate gives 2? Wait: quiet/quiet = 2 for me; submit/quiet = 0. If my policy is submit, other copy (same weights, same decision procedure) also submits → I get 4. If policy is pass, both pass → 2. 2 < 4, so defect (submit).\n\nWait — 4 years vs 2 years: submitting gives 4, mutual quiet gives 2. Fewer years better. Submit gives 0 if other passes. Mutual submit = 4. Mutual pass = 2. So cooperate (pass) better: 2 < 4. Yes, P-FDT recommends pass.\n\nAnswer: pass.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":6058,"completion_tokens":368,"total_tokens":6426,"cost":0.00103894,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":448,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00103894,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00085494,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.000184},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":167,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}